    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "rest doesn't fix it though. it's not just being tired. it feels more like... the well is just dry. permanent. i feel like i've spent my whole life trying to build something meaningful and i've just realized there's nothing left to build. it's just hollow now.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I hear you—this isn't fatigue, it's a deeper kind of loss, and pretending rest will cure it would be dishonest. But a dry well isn't always empty; sometimes it just needs a different digging spot, or time for the water table to shift. You don't have to rebuild meaning all at once—maybe just notice one small thing today that still feels real, even if it's just the weight of your own breath. That hollowness can be a threshold, not a tomb, even if it doesn't feel that way yet.",
